              {
                "text": "**Analyzing Triangle Beams**\n\nI'm currently considering a visual task featuring triangles. Each has a differently colored \"engine\" pixel, seemingly the source. The critical detail is the beam: does it shoot in the triangle's direction, its opposite, or through the apex? I need to analyze different triangle beam scenarios.\n\n\n**Investigating Beam Directions**\n\nI've been examining how the \"engine\" pixel (the source) in a triangle determines the beam's direction. For a triangle of 7s, I've confirmed the beam goes directly from the tip of the triangle, shooting outwards. It shoots from row 3 up to row 0. Now I'm analyzing a triangle of 4s, which points LEFT. The \"engine\" is a 1, and I see the beam travels left from the tip.\n\n\n",
                "type": "reasoning_text"
              }
            ],
            "encrypted_content": null,
